  "source_review": [
    "A single comparison_constant numeric helper serves all six operators from the existing producer visitor, only in Pine v6.",
    "Mixed finite int/float operands widen before nine-decimal rounding. Pure integer comparisons retain exact integer arithmetic; boolean comparisons retain their distinct path.",
    "Round_constant and its existing helper retain identical ASTs; only comparison_constant is added. Every binder method except _evaluate_const_node retains the identical AST.",
    "Finite float decimal ratios are bounded by the representation; explicit integer bit bounds and float overflow rejection avoid unbounded conversion. The existing visitor work/depth/cache/purity protections are unchanged.",
    "Exact decimal midpoint operands are left without constant evidence. The implementation does not borrow math.round tie semantics for the undocumented comparison midpoint rule.",
    "Known NA from a valid typed conditional becomes false for all six v6 operators; unknown value evidence and the unreviewed UDF NA path remain unknown. Invalid bare-NA draft examples are not counted as positive authority.",
    "The v5 path remains unchanged, and its preservation tests are not presented as historical comparison parity."
  ],
